  "$comment": "TASK-1005 — the platform-admin model-residency API, PINNED by the orchestrator before wave 2 so the controller lane (L-CTRL, producer) and the console lane (L-UI, consumer) build in parallel against the same shape. All routes are under /api/v1/admin/model-residency, platform-admin only (SUPER_ADMIN in a tenant-less context; tenants never see this surface — D-11), @ForbidApiKey, svc scope `svc:admin:model-residency:manage` for writes and `svc:admin:model-residency:read` for reads. `mode` is `shadow` until the SYSTEM setting `residency.enforce` is true. Every write is audited as a sys-event on ResourceType `ModelResidencyPolicy` (actions) — a force-load over budget REQUIRES a non-empty `reason` (owner OD-3) and answers 409 `OVER_BUDGET` without `force: true`. Unload with in-flight work answers 409 `IN_FLIGHT` unless `force: true`. Policy writes are OCC: `If-Match` required (428 missing, 412 drift). `models[].requestsPerMin` and `p50LatencyMs` come from Prometheus (`model_running_instances`, `model_inference_latency_seconds`) and may be null. `freshness.staleServices` lists services whose last agent report is older than 30 s. Error bodies follow the gateway house form: the object passed to Nest's ConflictException etc. — { code, message, ...details } — exactly like AGENT_CONNECTION_UNAVAILABLE.",
