    "$note": "ASYNCHRONOUS. A 5 GB LLM load takes ~100 s (TASK-1005 §10.1), past Cloudflare's 100 s edge timeout for a browser request, so the route answers 202 as soon as the load is admitted and the load runs in the background. Progress is read from GET (models[].state loading -> loaded, or the entry disappears on failure) and from GET /api/v1/admin/model-residency/operations/:operationId -> { id, action, service, modelRef, status: running|succeeded|failed, error: {code,message}|null, startedAt, finishedAt }. A model that is already resident answers 200 with `outcome: already_loaded` and the resident entry; no operation is created. A second load of the same model while one is running answers 409 LOAD_IN_PROGRESS. Unload is fast and stays synchronous (200).",
    "$optionsNote": "`options` is accepted ONLY for service `lm-studio` (400 OPTIONS_UNSUPPORTED otherwise) and carries exactly LM Studio REST v1's documented load keys (camelCased); anything the engine cannot take over REST (parallel slots, KV quantization, GPU split) is not expressible. `replace: true` = 'apply & reload': unload the resident instance(s) of this modelRef first, then load with `options`, as ONE operation (refused 409 IN_FLIGHT while the model serves requests unless `force: true`). Without `replace`, a resident model answers 200 `already_loaded` and `options` are ignored."
  },
